  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which builds the forest scene. It passes typecheck. I did not run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so I haven't seen it render. The scene has a 260×260 ground plane and 10,000 instanced objects in three draws: 8,000 trunks, 8,000 cone canopies and 2,000 rocks. Placement comes from a seeded LCG, so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours, and trunks share one brown. There is one shadow-casting directional light plus a hemisphere light, and exponential fog (`mode: \"exp\"`, density 0.0045). The camera is `camera.orbit` with `autoRotate` at 0.12 rad/s, positioned so the whole 75-unit-radius forest is in view. The engine owns the render loop. I added a separate `requestAnimationFrame` loop that sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` on its third tick, after `app.ready()`. That is a few frames after the first one, not on the exact first frame.",
